{
  "name": "404. AssemblyAI Sync API transcription: one upstream call, config part, duration usage, vendor errors (assemblyai transcription)",
  "description": "TXE-6435, contract C3, C4, C5, C6. The assemblyai provider transcribes with one call to AssemblyAI's Sync API (POST /v1/transcribe): the model is the X-AAI-Model header, the audio is the audio part and the request fields are the JSON config part; it never polls. 404.1 to 404.18 are a local fixture regression with no live provider call: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json (its assemblyai provider points at the fixture's /pp/assemblyai) and run with providerErrorFixture=1; they are skipped otherwise. The fixture answers /pp/assemblyai/v1/transcribe in the vendor's shape, counts each call under assemblyai:<model> and keeps what it received (GET /__assemblyai). 404.2 and 404.3 pin one request to one upstream call, the header, the two parts, the extra fields in the config unchanged, and usage{type: duration, seconds} = audio_duration_ms / 1000 with the vendor body in raw_response. 404.4 and 404.5 pin the same through the OpenAI drop-in route /openai/v1/audio/transcriptions, whose extra form fields and config object reach the config part. 404.6 and 404.7 pin the Gemini-shaped route /genai/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent with inline audio: the audio is the audio part and the request's text is the config prompt. 404.8 and 404.9 pin a vendor error: the vendor's status, its detail as the message, its title as the code, Retry-After as retry_after_ms and the error_type for the status. 404.10 to 404.13 pin that a field the Sync API cannot deliver (a subtitle response_format, the segment granularity, temperature on the drop-in route, and an audio url in place of the file) is a 400 caller_unsupported_parameter. 404.14 pins the shared extra-params rule (TXE-7018): language_codes sent as an extra field beside the unified language is a 400 caller_invalid_request naming it, never applied over the request's own field. 404.15 to 404.17 pin file_format: on the native route and on the drop-in route it names audio that has no signature (the fixture's text file standing in for raw PCM), the audio part is sent as audio/pcm, and file_format is not sent as a config member. 404.18 reads the counters: each vendor error reached the fixture once and the refused requests never did. The last case is live: it needs ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY and is skipped when the profile's key is unset. Before this provider existed the fork had no assemblyai provider, so none of these requests could be served.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "404.1 fixture counters reset before the assemblyai transcription rows",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('counters cleared', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json().data[0].reset, pm.response.text()).to.equal(true); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{providerErrorFixtureUrl}}/__reset"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "404.2 /v1/audio/transcriptions - transcript, words in seconds and usage.seconds = audio_duration_ms / 1000 - assemblyai/universal-3-5-pro",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "var j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('one Sync API response becomes the unified transcription', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  pm.expect(j.text, pm.response.text()).to.eql('The quick brown fox.');",
              "  pm.expect(j.usage, 'no usage: ' + pm.response.text()).to.be.an('object');",
              "  pm.expect(j.usage.type, pm.response.text()).to.eql('duration');",
              "  pm.expect(j.usage.seconds, 'audio_duration_ms 3312 / 1000: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(3.312);",
              "  pm.expect(j.duration, pm.response.text()).to.eql(3.312);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('word times are seconds, from the vendor milliseconds', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(j.words, 'no words: ' + pm.response.text()).to.be.an('array').with.lengthOf(4);",
              "  pm.expect(j.words[0], JSON.stringify(j.words[0])).to.deep.include({ word: 'The', start: 0.14, end: 0.26 });",
              "  pm.expect(j.words[3], JSON.stringify(j.words[3])).to.deep.include({ word: 'fox.', start: 0.9, end: 1.5 });",
              "});",
              "pm.test('the vendor body is returned raw and the named key served', function () {",
              "  var raw = j.extra_fields && j.extra_fields.raw_response;",
              "  pm.expect(raw, 'no raw_response: ' + pm.response.text()).to.be.an('object');",
              "  pm.expect(raw.audio_duration_ms, JSON.stringify(raw)).to.eql(3312);",
              "  pm.expect(raw.session_id, JSON.stringify(raw)).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-routing-info-provider'), 'provider header').to.eql('assemblyai');",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-routing-info-key'), 'key header').to.eql('assemblyai-fixture');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
